{"evidence_sentence":"Code E2101 is also covered for those with impairment of manual dexterity when the basic coverage criteria (1)-(2) are met and the treating practitioner certifies that the beneficiary has an impairment of manual dexterity severe enough to require the use of this special monitoring system. Coverage of code E2101 for beneficiaries with manual dexterity impairments is not dependent upon a visual impairment.","wording_differences":"Original: "Code E2101 is also covered for those with impairment of manual dexterity when the basic coverage criteria (1)-(2) are met and the treating practitioner certifies that the beneficiary has an impairment of manual dexterity severe enough to require the use of this special monitoring system."
Revised: "Code E2101 is also covered for those with impairment of manual dexterity when the basic coverage criteria (1)-(2) are met and the treating practitioner certifies that the beneficiary has an impairment of manual dexterity severe enough to require the use of this special monitoring system. Coverage of code E2101 for beneficiaries with manual dexterity impairments is not dependent upon a visual impairment."

The only difference is the addition of the clarifying sentence: "Coverage of code E2101 for beneficiaries with manual dexterity impairments is not dependent upon a visual impairment." Otherwise, the operative language is identical.","changes_what_claims_qualify":false,"verdict":"SUPPORTED","explanation":"The requirement that E2101 is covered for those with impairment of manual dexterity, when the basic coverage criteria are met and the practitioner certifies severity, is unchanged. The only addition is a clarifying sentence that coverage for manual dexterity impairment does not depend on visual impairment, which does not restrict or expand the original rule's scope. Therefore, the rule is still fully supported by the revised policy.","recommended_action":"KEEP"}
